      *> Report Writer Layer 2: PAGE LIMIT/FOOTING overflow -> flush page, new page, re-emit PAGE HEADING.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. P143.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT RPT ASSIGN "l2.txt" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL.
           SELECT RIN ASSIGN "l2.txt" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD RPT REPORT IS R.
       FD RIN.
       01 RR PIC X(20).
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 N PIC 99 VALUE 0.
       01 I PIC 99.
       01 E PIC X VALUE "N".
       REPORT SECTION.
       RD R PAGE LIMIT 6 LINE HEADING 1 FIRST DETAIL 3 FOOTING 5.
       01 TYPE PAGE HEADING.
          05 LINE 1. 10 COLUMN 1 PIC X(4) VALUE "PAGE".
       01 D TYPE DETAIL.
          05 LINE PLUS 1. 10 COLUMN 3 PIC 99 SOURCE N.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           OPEN OUTPUT RPT. INITIATE R.
           PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 6
              MOVE I TO N GENERATE D
           END-PERFORM.
           TERMINATE R. CLOSE RPT.
           OPEN INPUT RIN.
           PERFORM UNTIL E = "Y"
              READ RIN AT END MOVE "Y" TO E NOT AT END DISPLAY "[" RR "]" END-READ
           END-PERFORM.
           CLOSE RIN. STOP RUN.
